{# An American-style "work in progress" barricade planted on a zone under works
   (§ délais): a low, wide board with diagonal black/amber hazard stripes on two
   splayed A-frame legs. `phase` picks the local variant class (CVA-manuel, cf.
   CLAUDE.md §7): both phases are fully opaque — planned (during the lead: a
   chantier is reserved here, also why some tree choices are blocked) is static;
   active (the pose: the artisan is on site) gets a flashing amber beacon and a
   slight bob. Origin = ground midpoint between the two feet; the board stands
   above it. Colours/motion live in scene.css. Non-clickable (pointer-events
   none) so the zone underneath stays selectable. #}
{% props phase = 'planned' %}
<g class="chantier-marker chantier-marker--{{ phase }}"{{ attributes }}>
    <path class="cm-legs" d="M-15 -19 L-27 -1 M15 -19 L27 -1"/>
    <rect class="cm-board" x="-32" y="-33" width="64" height="13" rx="2"/>
    <circle class="cm-beacon" cx="0" cy="-37" r="3.2"/>
</g>
